<urn:wikibase:item:Item_11> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A comfortable Poké Ball that makes a caught wild Pokémon quickly grow friendly."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_24> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Fully restores HP."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_26> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Restores 60 HP."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_32> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Restores 70 HP."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_18> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A spray-type medicine. It lifts the effect of poison from one Pokémon."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_16> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A quite rare Poké Ball that has been specially crafted to commemorate an occasion of some sort."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_31> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Restores 50 HP."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_27> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A spray-type medicine. It heals all the status problems of a single Pokémon."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_99> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A fossil of an ancient Pokémon that lived in the sea. It appears to be part of a plant root."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_62> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Raises Special Defense of a Pokémon in battle."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_75> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A small green shard. It appears to be from some sort of implement made long ago."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_81> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Evolves certain species of Pokémon."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_65> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A toy flute made from blue glass. A maniac will buy it for a high price."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_20> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A spray-type medicine. It defrosts a Pokémon that has been frozen solid."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_93> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A pretty, heart-shaped scale that is extremely rare. It glows faintly in the colors of the rainbow."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_73> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A small blue shard. It appears to be from some sort of implement made long ago."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_56> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Raises critical-hit ratio of a Pokémon in battle."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_72> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A small red shard. It appears to be from some sort of implement made long ago."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_60> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Raises Accuracy of a Pokémon in battle."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_58> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Raises Defense of a Pokémon in battle."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A special Poké Ball that is used only in the Great Marsh. It is decorated in a camouflage pattern."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_83> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Evolves certain species of Pokémon."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_36> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Heals all status problems, but lowers Friendship."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_34> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Restores 60 HP but lowers Friendship."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_71> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A pretty seashell that can be found deep inside the Shoal Cave. A maniac will buy it for a high price."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_61> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Raises Special Attack of a Pokémon in battle."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_84> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Evolves certain species of Pokémon."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_85> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Evolves certain species of Pokémon."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_51> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "It slightly raises the maximum PP of a selected move that has been learned by the target Pokémon."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_63> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A doll that attracts Pokémon. Use it to flee from any battle with a wild Pokémon."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_40> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "It restores the PP of all the moves learned by the targeted Pokémon by 10 points each."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_28> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A medicine that revives a fainted Pokémon. It restores half the Pokémon's maximum HP."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_29> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A medicine that revives a fainted Pokémon. It fully restores the Pokémon's HP."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_33> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Milk with a very high nutrition content. It restores the HP of one Pokémon by 100 points."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_66> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A toy flute made from yellow glass. A maniac will buy it for a high price."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An ultra-performance Ball that provides a higher Pokémon catch rate than a Great Ball."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_98> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A fertilizer to be spread on soft soil in regions where Berries are grown. A maniac will buy it for a high price."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_39> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "It fully restores the PP of a single selected move that has been learned by the target Pokémon."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_76> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An item that prevents weak wild Pokémon from appearing for 200 steps after its use."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_54> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Heals all major status conditions."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_91> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A shard of a pretty gem that sparkles in a red color. It can be sold at a high price to shops."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A device for catching wild Pokémon. It is thrown like a ball at the target. It is designed as a capsule system."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_23> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A medicine that fully restores the HP and heals any status problems of a single Pokémon."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_64> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An item that attracts Pokémon. Use it to flee from any battle with a wild Pokémon."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_97> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A fertilizer to be spread on soft soil in regions where Berries are grown. A maniac will buy it for a high price."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_55> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Prevents stat reduction for five turns."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_9> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A somewhat different Poké Ball that works especially well on Pokémon species that were previously caught."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_10> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A somewhat different BALL that becomes progressively better the more turns there are in a battle."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_67> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A toy flute made from red glass. A maniac will buy it for a high price."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_46> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Increases Attack EVs by 10."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_8> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A somewhat different Poké Ball that works especially well on weaker Pokémon in the wild."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_13> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A somewhat different Poké Ball that makes it easier to catch wild Pokémon at night or in dark places like caves."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_30> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Restores 30 HP."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_90> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Lovely, red-colored sand with a loose, silky feel. It can be sold at a high price to shops."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_100> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A fossil of an ancient Pokémon that lived in the sea. It appears to be part of a claw."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_48> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Increases Speed EVs by 10."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The best Ball with the ultimate level of performance. It will catch any wild Pokémon without fail."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_52> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Increases Special Defense EVs by 10."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_6> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A somewhat different Poké Ball that works especially well on Water- and Bug-type Pokémon."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_50> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A candy that is packed with energy. It raises the level of a single Pokémon by one."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_88> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A somewhat-small pearl that sparkles in a pretty silver color. It can be sold cheaply to shops."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_74> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A small yellow shard. It appears to be from some sort of implement made long ago."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A good, high-performance Ball that provides a higher Pokémon catch rate than a standard Poké Ball."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_94> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A sweet honey with a lush aroma that attracts wild Pokémon when it is used in grass, caves, or on special trees."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_7> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A somewhat different Poké Ball that works especially well on Pokémon that live underwater."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_43> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A 100% pure juice made of Berries. It restores the HP of one Pokémon by just 20 points."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_78> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A long, durable rope. Use it to escape instantly from a cave or a dungeon."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_49> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Increases Special Attack EVs by 10."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_68> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A toy flute made from black glass. A maniac will buy it for a high price."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_82> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Evolves certain species of Pokémon."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_22> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A spray-type medicine. It eliminates paralysis from a single Pokémon."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_86> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A small and rare mushroom. It is sought after by collectors."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_79> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An item that prevents weak wild Pokémon from appearing for 100 steps after its use."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_95> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A fertilizer to be spread on soft soil in regions where Berries are grown. A maniac will buy it for a high price."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_89> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A quite-large pearl that sparkles in a pretty silver color. It can be sold at a high price to shops."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_92> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A nugget of pure gold that gives off a lustrous gleam. It can be sold at a high price to shops."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_41> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "It fully restores the PP of all the moves learned by the targeted Pokémon."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_53> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "It maximally raises the top PP of a selected move that has been learned by the target Pokémon."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_77> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An item that prevents weak wild Pokémon from appearing for 250 steps after its use."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_44> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "It revives all fainted Pokémon. In doing so, it also fully restores their HP."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_96> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A fertilizer to be spread on soft soil in regions where Berries are grown. A maniac will buy it for a high price."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_57> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Raises Attack of a Pokémon in battle."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_12> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A somewhat rare Poké Ball that has been specially made to commemorate an event of some sort."@en .
<urn:wikibase:item:Item_15> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A somewhat different Poké Ball that provides a better catch rate if it is used at the start of a wild encounter."@en .
